// AS-REP Roasting via Accounts Without Kerberos Pre-Authentication
// Detects Kerberos AS-REQ activity for accounts that have pre-authentication disabled. The KDC hands back an AS-REP encrypted with a key derived from the account password, which is then cracked offline. Deliberate use of DONT_REQ_PREAUTH is rare, so volume here is usually roasting.
// techniques: T1558.004   severity: high
// source: rules/credential-access/asrep-roasting-no-preauth.yml  (GENERATED, do not edit by hand)
SecurityEvent
| where (((EventID =~ "4768") and (TicketOptions =~ "0x40810010") and (TicketEncryptionType =~ "0x17" or TicketEncryptionType =~ "0x18")) and not ((TargetUserName endswith "$")))
